<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:55:07Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path, from crewed spaceflight to communications</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:324f88130f0700fb3f2f8483ac06dd4ce28e20ba5b2c7c1ad8cbe10f82098f14</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:03:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications--25ea30849574.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called on Thursday for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place against the United States and China in the space race, from communications to crewed spaceflight. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations, and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".</summary></entry><entry><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:099e45b9a4c448b5730caf2e2aa166d45a5ee5c3ad0db87b6568267f561a88e9</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush--ae85c7241bed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>International Space Summit: Europe plays catch-up with US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:684ec64e4f87b848d1e0ffbdbdbcb947269a73efd4784bda9c782a94fcaa4e55</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:28:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260910-international-space-summit-europe-plays-catch-up-with-us-and-china--975a45d2435a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260910-international-space-summit-europe-plays-catch-up-with-us-and-china" /><summary type="html">The space sector is booming. The global industry expected to reach a value of €2 trillion mark by 2040. But behind this spectacular growth lies major geopolitical challenges, particularly for Europe. In this edition, FRANCE 24’s Charles Pellegrin speaks to Kai-Uwe Schrogl at the International Space Summit in Paris. Schrogl, a political affairs adviser to the European Space Agency, answers questions about the future of the great beyond and Europe’s place in the new space race.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Russia tricks 'vulnerable' foreigners to fight in Ukraine war, Amnesty reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:050747628114ceb3d783c958b6a48174eae0bc095046525cbc46652a48e960f6</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-russia-tricks-vulnerable-foreigners-to-fight-in-ukraine-war-amnesty-reports--21a0ba2cee79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-russia-tricks-vulnerable-foreigners-to-fight-in-ukraine-war-amnesty-reports" /><summary type="html">Foreign nationals are being tricked into fighting for the Russian army against Ukraine through fake job offers, an Amnesty International report said Thursday, citing interviews with prisoners of war. The average targeted recruit is under 40, living in a poorer country and lured by the "promise of a job", Amnesty's secretary-general said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Revisited: Consequences of the 2022 Nord Stream pipeline sabotage are still being felt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09e809b2135d9dc45d2641d62272a78e6bdb179522973f32b1b0da1d724263cb</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:54:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:07:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260910-revisited-consequences-of-the-2022-nord-stream-pipeline-sabotage-are-still-being-felt--9c31cb3af302.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20260910-revisited-consequences-of-the-2022-nord-stream-pipeline-sabotage-are-still-being-felt" /><summary type="html">It is one of the most spectacular acts of sabotage committed since World War II. On the night of September 26, 2022, three of the four pipes of the Nord Stream 1 and Nord Stream 2 gas pipelines exploded on the seabed of the Baltic Sea. 465 thousand metric tons of methane were released into the atmosphere. The long-standing and strategic link between Russia and Germany severed for good.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>RN 'breach': Amid 'severe' differences with 'bright, young' Bardella, Le Pen 'dictates party line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:489035c117474a338aaaa69d5529b800ff6cf3788bc8d69871132bfa3019993a</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:55:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T12:25:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-rn-breach-amid-severe-differences-with-bright-young-bardella-le-pen-dictates-party-line-1--39a881e6ef18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-rn-breach-amid-severe-differences-with-bright-young-bardella-le-pen-dictates-party-line-1" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Mallet, Financial Times Senior Editor at the World News Desk. He interprets the emerging tensions between Marine Le Pen and Jordan Bardella as more than a clash of personalities. They reveal a deeper struggle over the political future of France's far-right National Rally is becoming as they find themselves in prime position in their hunt to capture the French presidency. Bardella is formally president of the party and has developed his own political constituency, particularly among younger voters and parts of the business community. Yet Mallet argues that Le Pen continues to exercise the decisive ideological and strategic authority.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bayeux Tapestry 'mania' sweeps UK as first exhibition outside France opens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1dfe9e5e8ecbf6fd9f463d5813f131e6118be58c6b0d23ae837d85887572e69</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:55:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T02:05:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-bayeux-tapestry-mania-sweeps-uk-as-first-exhibition-outside-france-opens--9986e6fe38f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-bayeux-tapestry-mania-sweeps-uk-as-first-exhibition-outside-france-opens" /><summary type="html">The British Museum on Thursday opened its doors for the first public display of the 1,000-year-old Bayeux Tapestry outside of France. The museum has so far sold a record-breaking 100,000 tickets to see the tapestry, which depicts the Norman conquest of England under William the Conqueror.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Passengers or pilots?' Europe looks to challenge US dominance in space sector with €10 billion plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62f9e5327c5692e88520154317b9976ab8c492c6a3a644bb7577dde9aa38292c</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:55:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:56:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-passengers-or-pilots-europe-looks-to-challenge-us-dominance-in-space-sector-with-_10-billio--9d31a0c4aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-passengers-or-pilots-europe-looks-to-challenge-us-dominance-in-space-sector-with-%E2%82%AC10-billion-plan" /><summary type="html">Key figures from Europe’s space industry and other international players have converged on Paris to discuss how to advance the continent’s ambitions in a global market dominated by the United States.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU gives Spain 115 mn euros aid over Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee0e2ee7c85af5dc09b0b403eb5589e60f382346106b5168b4833d3347533a54</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:06:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis--38a16ccc97da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-gives-spain-115-mn-euros-aid-over-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">The EU on Wednesday said it was granting Spain 115 million euros ($130 million) in emergency aid to help bolster border security and assist returns after the massive migrant rush into the north African exclave. More than 70,000 migrants crossed into Spanish territory from Morocco on July 30 and 31 in an unprecedented rush that left scores dead, most by drowning as they tried to swim around a breakwater. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rungis market chief on supply chains and feeding the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24924d92dee35f152a4c28ea6bdd9c8cf23ab22ff1a7b0ad122abcea4778abb5</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:05:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world--b449a157d7e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260909-rungis-market-chief-on-supply-chains-and-feeding-the-world" /><summary type="html">In today’s edition, FRANCE 24’s Delano D'Souza speaks with the man at the heart of France's food supply chain. Stéphane Layani is the head of the Rungis wholesale food market – the largest of its kind in Europe – and chairman of the World Union of Wholesale Markets. Earlier this year Layani came out with a book titled Le Monde a faim, or "The World is Hungry" in English. In his interview, he gives his perspective on how France's food system will transform in the coming years.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic calls snap elections after nearly two years of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:131e1dba88cd207dd3df59bc8b07c5075916af63e02dc9354984f871a6b9b9f2</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:15:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests--5f70b882a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-serbia-vucic-calls-snap-elections-after-nearly-two-years-protests" /><summary type="html">Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic on Wednesday called snap parliamentary elections for October 25. They are expected to be a key test of his right-wing populist Serbian Progressive Party after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strike near Ukraine-Moldova border kills at least two as Ukraine targets oil terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f22ea4d2c5c03f136a6cee9ed5d87df1ed5cdeef2773e875177b43e08b54d8</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:51:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-ter--fc9e4da4f8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-russian-drone-strike-near-ukraine-moldova-border-kills-at-least-two-as-ukraine-hits-oil-terminal" /><summary type="html">An overnight Russian drone strike at a border crossing between Ukraine and Moldova killed at least two people, Odesa's regional governor said Wednesday. Moldovan Prime Minister Vasile Tofan said that 17 drones had hit Moldovan territory in August alone as both Kyiv and Moscow ramp up long-range strikes on military and energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Travellers in UK face ongoing disruption after air traffic control glitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea87a311684be06e5847f22d8c7d77e73df4354b0481dfb360dfb37dde22f06e</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T03:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch--92d15f16fe8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260909-travellers-in-uk-face-ongoing-disruption-after-air-traffic-control-glitch" /><summary type="html">Flights from British airports began to resume Wednesday after a glitch in the country's air traffic control service left hundreds of thousands of passengers stranded and 2,000 cancellations, costing airlines millions of pounds. Authorities warned that travellers would continue to experience delays as airlines scrambled to recover from the outage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump tells Putin he wants swift end to Ukraine war, Kremlin says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5482155f45e4756fa3f9f910356a4e6c8abfb54489ed50fd9279135745862d8</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T19:07:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says--5f2aae4d01c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-trump-tells-putin-he-wants-swift-end-to-ukraine-war-kremlin-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump told Russian President Vladimir Putin he wanted a swift end to the Ukraine war, the Kremlin said, arguing that peace could pave the way for a broad restoration of US-Russia ties. The hour-long call Tuesday followed weekend talks by US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Moscow and Kyiv to try to revive stalled peace efforts.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Missiles or mediation? Trump envoys shuttle between Russia and Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ff7f8fd047f69f7506923c7bbf86ed43ff86b8a15634b83b0803399c715550f</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine--b5fc503da412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260908-missiles-or-mediation-trump-envoys-shuttle-between-russia-and-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s momentum on the battlefield was a primary focus at July’s NATO summit in Turkey. Kyiv’s long-range drones and US President Donald Trump’s surprise announcement that the Washington would allow Ukraine to produce Patriot missiles on in the country. However, Trump's deal has yet to materialize. Moreover, Russia has ramped up cruise missile launches and Ukraine has run out of air defenses to stop them. Moscow is also failing to stop incoming missiles. In today’s edition we ask: What happens in war when offense proves better than defense for both sides?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cbfcaefa8594cdfb9af054c6a563a44f8fc960ee05cc2ca3c441709cb494b3e</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower reopens after row over limits on women staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1b2dd5b015f4fba0c96454c364ec33b721429364f72ff8e942560ef1e17d4a5</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T15:18:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff--477be6cb13b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-eiffel-tower-reopens-after-row-over-limits-on-women-staff" /><summary type="html">The Eiffel Tower reopened Tuesday, a day after one of the world's most-visited landmarks was closed by a strike to protest what a union official called "unacceptable" management instructions limiting the presence of women during a visit by a Hindu religious group close to Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s ruling nationalist party.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spoiler alert: AI in cinema 'just a tool, won’t replace actors and human beings'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a57f00a31016f62765a1deca732af6ee53bc69314493c660b39d64348c61b4f</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:11:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1--59df42aa2e9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome film producer Lahoucine Grimich. He challenges the prevailing narrative that cinema is an industry in existential crisis. While acknowledging that viewing habits have dramatically shifted since the pandemic, he argues that streaming platforms, public support and theatrical exhibition are not competing forces. As demonstrated in the French model, they form parts of an interconnected financing ecosystem in which cinema can adapt without ever abandoning the big screen. He frames filmmaking as a form of cultural sovereignty: societies need films not simply as entertainment, but to recognise themselves and to create what he calls “new imaginaries.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Kyiv, ending three-day halt for US talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce3c6e28a6b316dc82a54e702e8af63ec52bb1b9f97564efc00ae3d95504aa4a</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:35:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-russia-pounds-kyiv-ending-three-day-halt-for-us-talks--d105618bccd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-russia-pounds-kyiv-ending-three-day-halt-for-us-talks" /><summary type="html">Russian missiles and drones pounded Kyiv overnight, killing two people and sending smoke billowing above the Ukrainian capital, ending Moscow's temporary halt to strikes on the city.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Ukraine, teens try to heal from trauma of war at summer camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a357ea5d31106d2c8db87588d188b9cc280c4350d5f5a0fb4ab7d1b4ec7f809</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:10:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260908-in-ukraine-teens-try-to-heal-from-trauma-of-war-at-summer-camp--b5b19daa74ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260908-in-ukraine-teens-try-to-heal-from-trauma-of-war-at-summer-camp" /><summary type="html">The psychological impact on the Ukrainian population of nearly five years of full-scale Russian onslaught is hard to overstate. Children and teenagers are particularly at risk of trauma. With support from foreign philanthropists, one Ukrainian NGO is trying to help at least a few teenagers cope better, via summer camps that mix therapy and fun. Our correspondent Gulliver Cragg reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>French police hunt Renoir thieves after lightning museum heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:555aa922675459fefb12c03ce5e96e2c0f2346b7818f86eb5c8a1c30918d1197</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T08:36:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-thieves-steal-works-of-art-worth-9-million-euros-from-france-s-renoir-museum--54621680077e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-thieves-steal-works-of-art-worth-9-million-euros-from-france-s-renoir-museum" /><summary type="html">Two thieves climbed through a window and stole four valuable Renoir paintings on Tuesday from the Renoir Museum in the town of Cagnes-sur-Mer on the French Riviera, but abandoned two of the artworks as they fled, authorities said. Investigators have launched a national search for the perpetrators.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French AI startup Mistral valued at over 21 billion euros after latest funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab36a37694e144d3c0d63cef44a7b988d27a15d42afb22d2221a2e17c53911db</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:03:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-french-ai-startup-mistral-raises-3-billion-euros-after-latest-funding--93b791671133.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-french-ai-startup-mistral-raises-3-billion-euros-after-latest-funding" /><summary type="html">French AI company Mistral announced Tuesday that it had raised three billion euros ($3.5 billion) in what it described as the largest-ever European tech fundraising, valuing the startup at over 21 billion euros. While still an upstart compared to the AI giants OpenAI or Anthropic, Mistral says it is carving a niche by offering models that companies can run themselves with their own data.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Putin tells Trump that Russia has no 'aggressive plans' towards Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe35448d8c8cc82305f4beab785f9ca1fef962ac6218a1ed02d1796fc5a026c6</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T02:00:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt--c216aa8a2eec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260908-live-russia-resumes-strikes-on-kyiv-after-three-day-halt" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin and his counterpart Donald Trump held a “constructive” phone call Tuesday during which the Russian leader emphasised that Moscow had “no aggressive plans towards Europe”, the Kremlin said. The call followed a visit to Moscow by US envoys for talks at ending the war in Ukraine. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU says no place for 'glorification of war criminals' as Mladic buried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2962da943164fdf754d383cbf2d7e292866a417a3c24558ca17fad42102eb946</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T21:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-says-no-place-for-glorification-of-war-criminals-as-mladic-buried--c505261200fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-no-place-for-glorification-of-war-criminals-as-mladic-buried" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Monday denounced any "glorification" of convicted war criminal Ratko Mladic in Serbia, as thousands gathered in Belgrade for his funeral. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Only the beginning? German far right's breakthrough shakes Europe to its core</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:687ebf409debbaae8d899780ce13e0724d49e9df0ae57564afa75f846c6a7b5f</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T19:38:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core--984465a67934.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260907-only-the-beginning-german-far-right-s-breakthrough-shakes-europe-to-its-core" /><summary type="html">The result was not enough to win outright, but certainly enough to shake Germany and Europe to their core: the far-right Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) trounced the ruling conservatives in the impoverished former East German state of Saxony-Anhalt in Sunday's election. We ask about the consequences of voting for an anti-immigrant, pro-Russian party that wants schools to teach less about the ills of Hitler and more about the glory of Bismarck.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'What we see right now is that Putin has zero interest in ending the war', Ukrainian MP Yasko says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecc3fdd634b2abd2e79b1a59b31241e4567485b33bbc28b5343a614f39c88b3b</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:38:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says--3db6e994afb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff on Monday touted progress in weekend discussions with Ukraine and Russia, raising the prospect of reviving three-way peace talks to end Europe's deadliest conflict since World War II. Ukrainian MP Lisa Yasko says that "we don't trust these talks", describing the US envoys' flattery towards Russian President Vladimir Putin as "disgraceful".</summary></entry><entry><title>Avalanche kills at least 11 climbers in southern Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89330cbc6455ebfbd506518d4dfcbf6e510f4a9b6ff6ce126b2156639a3e1b08</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:00:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia--cc82d0868712.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia" /><summary type="html">⁠At least ​11 people were killed and six ​others injured after an avalanche struck a group of climbers in Russia's ​southern Kabardino-Balkaria ‌Republic, local emergency services said. The ‌avalanche swept down Mount Mizhirgi, ⁠one of the highest peaks in Russia's North Caucasus.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1d32ecce8d2d57fab5a5f5dad1c1bdcea59ce189e78700cf085b45060252fb1</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1--3d84be7d1802.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.</summary></entry><entry><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75eb937a1f1117856993f7fdd435e4acadcc86ab7a246882d0a037d55b75e48c</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:45:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd--3acc1083cc66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd" /><summary type="html">Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa12b7441f4df1b59bb3a7d4739682df6eaaa5e39b86f524c1d3a431cc7488d0</id><updated>2026-09-11T04:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1--355f2ad6ae17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties.</summary></entry></feed>
